Meanwhile I got the answers: Sam switched to private mail since he was
thinking the whole threat is going to be more and more OT. He told me how
to display a file produced by vcsa and even how to extract plain ASCII
from a file containing IBMgraphics code.

For the sake of completeness here it is:

tail -c +5 | awk 'BEGIN { RS = ".."; ORS = ""; }
{ print substr( RT, 1, 1 ); }'

(Filename has to be inserted between tail -c +5 and the pipe)

